# Run with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client):
# click "Send Request" above a request, or press Ctrl+Alt+R.
# Start the server first: scripts/start-server.sh
#
# The MCP endpoint is stateless: each request stands alone, so you can send
# them in any order. apiKey comes from rest-client.environmentVariables in
# .vscode/settings.json, which holds the placeholder key from .env.example;
# if your .env sets another key, set apiKey in your user settings instead.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Initialize: the server reports its name and version
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "rest-client", "version": "0" }
  }
}

### List tools: ping is listed
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "tools/list" }

### Call ping: replies "pong"
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "method": "tools/call", "params": { "name": "ping", "arguments": {} } }

### Without the API key: 401 unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "method": "tools/list" }
